&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Tax Operations and Delivery team protects user trust by enabling accurate, reliable, and scalable tax operations supporting the TaxJar and Stripe Tax products. We partner closely with Product, Engineering, and cross-functional teams to solve operational challenges, support new capabilities, and continuously improve how tax operations are delivered.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As our products, partnerships, and operational footprint continue to grow, how we execute becomes just as important as what we execute. The Operations Program Management role exists to strengthen how Tax Operations and Delivery plans, coordinates, and delivers strategic work by building repeatable operating mechanisms that improve alignment, clarity, and execution across the team and its partners. If you’re energized by improving how teams work, bringing structure to ambiguity, and building scalable ways for teams to execute together, you’ll have the opportunity to shape the future of Tax Operations.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for an Operations Program Manager to help improve how Tax Operations and Delivery executes. You’ll partner across Tax Operations, Product, Engineering, and other cross-functional stakeholders to design and operationalize repeatable execution mechanisms that improve planning, coordination, and delivery for key initiatives.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is ideal for someone who enjoys bringing structure to ambiguity, simplifying complex organizational challenges, and building practical solutions that improve how teams work together. Your impact will be measured by the repeatable mechanisms you build that make operational excellence easier to achieve across the team.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, maintain, and improve repeatable, lightweight execution mechanisms that track program status, communicate progress, surface execution risks on a regular cadence, and escalate blockers to the appropriate stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with your immediate Ops team and one or two cross-functional leads across Tax Operations, Product, and Engineering to improve cross-functional planning, alignment, and execution of strategic initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify execution friction, process gaps, and process breakdowns, and recommend scalable improvements that strengthen operational effectiveness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish meaningful metrics and reporting that provide visibility into execution health and support data-informed decision making&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Facilitate cross-functional reviews, planning sessions, and execution forums that help teams align, resolve blockers, and deliver measurable outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor initiatives through rollout, evaluate outcomes, and drive follow-up improvements or remediation where needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of demonstrated experience leading complex cross-functional initiatives from ambiguity to execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to identify friction and design scalable improvements that drive measurable outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong structured problem-solving and diagnostic thinking skills, with the ability to investigate issues, identify root causes, and design scalable solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to influence stakeholders and drive alignment without direct authority&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing or improving operational processes, governance, or execution mechanisms that increased organizational effectiveness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience partnering closely with Product, Engineering, and Operations teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience establishing operating rhythms, planning processes, or organizational governance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in a high-growth SaaS, fintech, or operationally complex environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with operational readiness, launch management, or change management practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using operational metrics to measure execution health and drive continuous improvement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with AI, automation, or workflow tools to improve organizational effectiveness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lean Six Sigma, continuous improvement, or systems thinking experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;About Zipline&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Zipline is the world’s largest and most experienced drone delivery service. We are on a mission to serve all humans equally by ensuring access to food, medicine and essential goods anytime, anywhere. We design, build, and operate the world’s largest autonomous logistics system, delivering critical supplies quickly and reliably. Today, Zipline operates on four continents, makes a delivery somewhere in the world every 30 seconds, and has completed millions of deliveries to date, including blood, vaccines, medical supplies, food, and retail products.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our customers include the world’s largest and most prominent healthcare systems, governments, retailers, restaurants and global businesses who rely on us to save lives, reduce emissions, increase economic opportunity, and provide delivery from point A to point B as fast as possible. The drone is only 15% of what we’ve built to enable seamless, reliable, global operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our system strengthens supply chains, reduces congestion, and gives people time back. With more than 140 million commercial autonomous miles safely flown, Zipline is redefining access to healthcare, consumer products, and food across the globe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We operate at a global scale and are looking for practical problem solvers who thrive on real-world challenges and rapid growth. Our team is motivated by building systems that have a direct, meaningful impact on people’s lives and by scaling the future of logistics. We are seeking people who sculpt from first principles, enjoy facing adversity, and can do the impossible at record breaking speeds.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About You and The Role&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;104&quot;&gt;Zipline’s Integration, Quality, Production, and Manufacturing Engineering organization turns complex hardware designs into safe, high-quality products that can be manufactured reliably at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;300&quot;&gt;As the Senior/Staff Technical Program Manager for Manufacturing Strategy &amp;amp; Operations, you will serve as a strategic partner to the Director and leadership team. You will translate manufacturing goals into clear strategies, analytical decisions, operating plans, and cross-functional execution.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;596&quot;&gt;The organization is entering a period of significant growth in production capacity, factory footprint, organizational complexity, and team scope. You will help guide that growth by developing capacity and labor plans, leading strategic analyses, improving executive communication, and driving high-priority projects from concept through implementation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;950&quot;&gt;This is not a traditional program coordination role. You will independently structure ambiguous problems, build rigorous analyses, develop recommendations, and help leaders make faster, better-informed decisions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Develop Manufacturing Strategy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;ul1&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Build manufacturing growth plans that connect production demand, factory capacity, labor, equipment, facilities, quality, and organizational capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Translate production ramps into recommendations for facility footprint, shifts, hiring, training, equipment, and investment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Develop scenario models that evaluate demand, productivity, yield, automation, outsourcing, cost, and schedule risk.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Support annual planning, headcount planning, budgeting, capital planning, and organizational design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Enable Leadership Decisions&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;ul1&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Turn complex operational questions into clear analyses, tradeoffs, and recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Develop business cases for major investments, organizational changes, and strategic initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Prepare executive presentations, decision documents, operating reviews, and strategic communications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Establish a consistent source of truth for performance, capacity, staffing, priorities, risks, and commitments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build the Operating System&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;ul1&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Design operating rhythms that connect long-range strategy to weekly and monthly execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Establish metrics and dashboards across safety, quality, production, engineering, capacity, labor, cost, and schedule.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Create clear mechanisms for escalating decisions, assigning owners, and driving actions through closure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Improve communication between functional teams, organizational leadership, and senior executives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead Strategic Programs&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;ul1&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Own high-priority initiatives that span multiple teams or lack a clear functional owner.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Lead programs such as factory labor-model changes, organizational transformations, and productivity efforts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Coordinate across Production, Manufacturing Engineering, Quality, Integration, Supply Chain, Finance, People, Recruiting, Facilities, and Design Engineering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Identify systemic blockers, drive cross-functional decisions, and ensure execution against agreed plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Increase Leadership Leverage&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;ul1&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Serve as a trusted thought partner to the Director and leadership team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Translate leadership discussions into clear strategies, decisions, communications, and action plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Maintain continuity across meetings by tracking decisions, dependencies, and follow-through.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Identify recurring coordination work and build more scalable systems and ownership models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;ul1&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;7+ years of experience in technical program management, manufacturing strategy, business operations, industrial engineering, manufacturing engineering, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Experience in a complex hardware, manufacturing, aerospace, automotive, robotics, medical-device, or similarly technical environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Demonstrated ability to structure ambiguous problems and translate quantitative and qualitative analysis into clear recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Experience developing capacity plans, labor models, operational strategies, organizational plans, or business cases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Strong understanding of manufacturing concepts such as capacity, takt time, throughput, yield, labor utilization, equipment constraints, and production readiness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Experience leading complex cross-functional initiatives through implementation and measurable results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Exceptional written and verbal communication skills, including executive-level presentations and decision documents.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Advanced proficiency with Excel or Google Sheets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Ability to influence senior leaders and cross-functional partners without direct authority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Work in a factory environment - onsite role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;ul1&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Bachelor’s degree in engineering, industrial/systems engineering, operations, business, economics, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Experience supporting a major production ramp, factory expansion, or rapidly scaling organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Experience in a chief-of-staff, strategy and operations, or business operations role within a technical organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Experience with headcount planning, organizational design, budgeting, capital planning, or financial modeling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Familiarity with Lean Manufacturing or other high-rate manufacturing systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Success in the First 30/90/180 Days&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;First 30 Days&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;ul1&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Develop a strong understanding of the organization, production system, priorities, and scaling risks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Build relationships with functional leaders and key cross-functional partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Take ownership of core organizational communications and recurring operating reviews.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;First 90 Days&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;ul1&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Establish a clear organizational scorecard and leadership operating cadence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Deliver an integrated manufacturing and labor scaling model.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Lead one high-priority strategic project from problem definition through an approved execution plan.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;First 180 Days&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class=&quot;ul1&quot;&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Deliver a 12–24 month manufacturing and organizational strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Establish reliable planning and communication systems that improve decision-making.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;li1&quot;&gt;Execute a major initiative that measurably improves capacity, productivity, cost, quality, or organizational readiness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Else You Need To Know&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Zipline is an equal opportunity employer and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any type without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, national origin, disability status, genetics, protected veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state or local laws or our own sensibilities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We value diversity at Zipline and welcome applications from those who are traditionally underrepresented in tech. If you like the sound of this position but are not sure if you are the perfect fit, please apply!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h3 class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Voluntary Self-Identification&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;For government reporting purposes, we ask candidates to respond to the below self-identification survey. Completion of the form is entirely voluntary. Whatever your decision, it will not be considered in the hiring process or thereafter. Any information that you do provide will be recorded and maintained in a confidential file.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p2&quot;&gt;As set forth in Zipline ’s Equal Employment Opportunity policy, we do not discriminate on the basis of any protected group status under any applicable law.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
